From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:16:50 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Keep the port when the local host name does not resolve

getLocalAddress() returned early without setting the port or the address
when gethostname() or gethostbyname() failed, and its callers don't check
the result: the server URL printed whatever was on the stack, and the LAN
session search sent its localhost request there. Set the port and the
loopback address before looking up the host name.

This also made the "NetPeer - Local Address" test fail in build
environments whose host name is not resolvable.
---
 engine/Poseidon/Network/Legacy/NetPeer.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/engine/Poseidon/Network/Legacy/NetPeer.cpp b/engine/Poseidon/Network/Legacy/NetPeer.cpp
index ad3d263..2f8cddb 100644
--- a/engine/Poseidon/Network/Legacy/NetPeer.cpp
+++ b/engine/Poseidon/Network/Legacy/NetPeer.cpp
@@ -74,6 +74,9 @@ const char* BreakFileName = "break.txt";
 bool getLocalAddress(struct sockaddr_in& me, unsigned16 port)
 {
     me.sin_family = AF_INET;
+    me.sin_port = htons(port);
+    // Callers use the address without checking for failure: leave them a valid one
+    me.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl(INADDR_LOOPBACK);
     char meName[128];
     if (gethostname(meName, 128) == SOCKET_ERROR)
     {
@@ -119,7 +122,6 @@ bool getLocalAddress(struct sockaddr_in& me, unsigned16 port)
     {
         me.sin_addr.s_addr = inet_addr(meName);
     }
-    me.sin_port = htons(port);
 #ifdef NET_LOG_GET_LOCAL_ADDRESS
     NetLog("getLocalAddress: local port: %u", (unsigned)port);
 #endif
